# CSS Philosophy

Prefer simple, maintainable CSS architecture.

Avoid overengineering styling systems prematurely.

---

# Styling

Prefer:
- component-scoped CSS
- predictable class names
- readable layout structure

Avoid deeply nested selectors.

---

# Layout

Prefer:
- flexbox
- grid

for layout systems.

Avoid fragile positioning hacks.

---

# Responsiveness

Design mobile-first when possible.

Ensure layouts adapt cleanly across screen sizes.

---

# Animations

Keep transitions subtle and purposeful.

Avoid excessive animation.

---

# Maintainability

Keep styles close to related components.

Extract repeated patterns into reusable utility classes only when justified.